1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:04,020 --> 00:00:09,860
Finally, after 10,000 years in exile,
the mighty Leviathan is ready to return.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,852
But in order to reach his full potential,

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,200
there are several souls
that must still be offered.

5
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,200
Now then, on to phase two.

6
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:24,980
Each glimmer of light
must join to become whole.

7
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,037
Each soul must be utilized.

8
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:32,060
Only then can the Leviathan cross over.

9
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:36,280
Ancient soldiers of the
Orychalcos, hear me!

10
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:40,340
Locate the scattered pieces
of the Great Leviathan,

11
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,320
for the Battle of Atlantis begins again!

12
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:51,720
Yes, my Orychalcos soldiers.

13
00:00:53,860 --> 00:00:56,657
Scatter your forces to the
far corners of the earth

14
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:00,000
and deliver to me all
the souls you can gather.

15
00:01:03,360 --> 00:01:05,200
This is Valon. Go ahead.

16
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:08,920
The Pharaoh's friends are
heading your way. Good.

17
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:12,236
Then it's time for me to
show Joey Wheeler who's boss.

18
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:18,270
Look!

19
00:01:18,353 --> 00:01:19,183
Here comes Joey!

20
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:22,660
And there he goes! Hey! Come back!

21
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:24,428
You're going the wrong way!

22
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:30,975
I'm coming for your thoughts, and I'm
not leaving without Yu-Gi and Mai!

23
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,820
Joey, come back!

24
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:40,216
I'm wearing the wrong shoes for this.

25
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,620
Joey, stop! Yeah!

26
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:45,600
What's that?

27
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:48,220
Uh, Joey? Yeah?

28
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,518
Maybe we should start running again.

29
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:54,740
Hey, stop!

30
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:57,480
Ever hear of looking both ways?

31
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,340
Hey, hold on!

32
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,148
You're going the wrong way!

33
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,360
Turn back!

34
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:05,110
Oh, me!

35
00:03:07,460 --> 00:03:08,677
It's just a dream.

36
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,140
It's just a dream.

37
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,720
See ya.

38
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,800
We'll never outrun this thing.

39
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:24,690
Joey!

40
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:30,980
You beat him.

41
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:33,660
Actually, I think he did.

42
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,240
Hold on.

43
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:36,440
I know that guy.

44
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,337
He's the one that took mine.

45
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:39,680
Right, you are, mate.

46
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:41,940
Hey, come back!

47
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:43,320
Joey, not again!

48
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,660
Come back!

49
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,700
This will do the trick.

50
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:52,180
Now, time to chase him down and save mine.

51
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:54,780
Are you nuts?

52
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,800
I guess so.

53
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,060
He's riding right into a trap.

54
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,740
Guess who, pal?

55
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:15,100
I'm on you like stink on an elephant.

56
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,000
Hey, you!

57
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:20,220
You're not getting away that easily. Hey!

58
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,720
Hey! Shit!

59
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,260
I don't think so.

60
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,190
Hey!

61
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:34,250
Shit!

62
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,340
Very funny!

63
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,860
Your turn, Wheeler!

64
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:07,140
Here goes!

65
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,040
Come on!

66
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,680
What, that's it?

67
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:24,920
So, you want a little
more, do you? Well, hey!

68
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:26,060
Let's go!

69
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:33,600
Where are those two already?

70
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,580
Right over there!

71
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,430
Hey, guys!

72
00:05:40,513 --> 00:05:41,420
You made it!

73
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,682
We were worried about you
two for a second there.

74
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,100
We're fine.

75
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:51,831
And now that we know who we're after,
it's time to crash their little party.

76
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,997
Well, we better act fast,

77
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:57,660
because Joey ran off to find
these Paradeus guys on his own.

78
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,978
We have to get there before he does.

79
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:02,440
He better not screw this up for me.

80
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,780
Hey, we've got bigger problems, guys.

81
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:10,017
Guys, those same monsters we saw
in the desert are roaming the city.

82
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,300
Oh, no. Let's go.

83
00:06:11,500 --> 00:06:13,720
We can all jump in my car. Good idea.

84
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:17,656
I'm afraid things are even
worse than you can imagine.

85
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:18,918
What is it, Gramps?

86
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,006
What do these creatures want?

87
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,557
According to the evening news,

88
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:26,257
thousands of people around the
world are suddenly collapsing

89
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:29,577
in the streets and falling into
a state of unconsciousness.

90
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,836
It's those monsters.

91
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:35,355
They must be using the power of the
Orikalkos to capture people's souls.

92
00:06:35,780 --> 00:06:38,060
It would appear so. Oh,

93
00:06:38,300 --> 00:06:42,757
and did I mention that every police officer
in this town is under their spell, too?

94
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:43,670
All right.

95
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:47,957
Then we have to battle these monsters
on our own and make our way to darts.

96
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,900
Unless he finds us first!

97
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:05,300
Keep fighting, my soldiers.

98
00:07:05,780 --> 00:07:10,037
We must continue to collect
the souls of man and beast

99
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:14,340
until we have amassed enough
power to rebuild Atlantis.

100
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:23,410
Joey!

101
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:24,800
Where are you?

102
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,140
Is that you, Joey?

103
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:33,660
Not quite.

104
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,620
But I am looking for him.

105
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:36,610
Look, my...

106
00:07:36,693 --> 00:07:37,523
Save it, dweeb.

107
00:07:37,606 --> 00:07:39,737
I know you're his
babysitter, so where is he?

108
00:07:39,820 --> 00:07:41,020
How should I know?

109
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:46,540
One of your little pals forced him into a
game of cat and mouse, and now he's gone.

110
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:48,320
It's Valon.

111
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,500
This is all your fault, my.

112
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,857
You're the one who got Joey into
this mess in the first place.

113
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:54,770
Out of my way.

114
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,460
Get back here.

115
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:59,112
The last thing he needs right now is you.

116
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,380
Here we are, old chum.

117
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,060
Glad you could make it.

118
00:08:11,340 --> 00:08:14,000
Now let's get down to business, shall we?

119
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:16,080
Look, pal, I want my back.

120
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:17,640
Then why chase me?

121
00:08:17,980 --> 00:08:20,477
She happens to have a
mind of her own, you know.

122
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:21,390
She did.

123
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:22,517
At least...

124
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:25,180
She did before you guys brainwashed her!

125
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,773
You don't get it, mate.

126
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:28,560
No one was brainwashed.

127
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:32,360
Ma chose to join our side
with her own free will.

128
00:08:32,540 --> 00:08:33,557
And you want to know why?

129
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:37,287
She was sick of taking a back
seat while you got all the fame.

130
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:39,994
Then I stepped in and changed all that.

131
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,237
You messed with her head.

132
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,496
That's what you did.

133
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:44,800
She was one of my best friends.

134
00:08:45,020 --> 00:08:49,902
But the last time I saw her, she was saying
things that mine never would have said.

135
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:54,340
I was sick of my life,
so I chose to change it.

136
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:55,720
No way!

137
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,060
How could you?

138
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,500
You guys wouldn't understand.

139
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:02,757
You've never been an outsider like me.

140
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:07,680
You've got your little group
and I'm not part of it Wake up,

141
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:10,917
Wheeler I led you here
to get rid of you for

142
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,800
good Cause Mai can't be
happy with you around Eh?

143
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,277
And what does that mean?

144
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,897
You're a constant reminder
of what her life used

145
00:09:18,980 --> 00:09:22,297
to be And Mai wants to
forget all that But as long

146
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:24,717
as you still exist in
this world She'll never be

147
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:28,240
able to forget So I'm
here to erase you for good

148
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:32,480
Plus I know that deep
down Mai still loves you

149
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:35,180
And I can't have that.

150
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:37,127
So what do you say, Wheeler?

151
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:39,540
Do we have ourselves a duel or not?

152
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,412
Not that I'm giving you much of a choice.

153
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:50,020
I never back down from a challenge,
especially when I'm fighting for a friend.

154
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:51,382
Now let's duel!

155
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:56,020
You're going down.

156
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:57,360
My move.

157
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,820
Check this out.

158
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,960
I summon alligator sword.

159
00:10:04,800 --> 00:10:06,120
Hey, gotta be careful.

160
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:09,538
I don't know anything about
this guy's dueling style.

161
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,520
Nice opening card.

162
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,428
Unfortunately for you,
mine is better, mate.

163
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:17,040
Just take a look.

164
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:19,720
It's my good friend, Psychic Armahead.

165
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:21,160
Psycho Armah who?

166
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,480
What's that do?

167
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:24,740
You're about to find out.

168
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:33,282
Did you just summon a monster that has zero
attack points or am I imagining things?

169
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:34,250
You're right,

170
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:38,777
my psychic armor head doesn't have
a single attack point But when I add

171
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:43,120
it together with a few other cards
it becomes my very own suit of armor

172
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:48,920
And here's the piece that'll hold it all
together, my armored gravitation card

173
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,837
I'm gonna need a little
more information here

174
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:55,020
My Tramp Buster armor
should clear things up.

175
00:10:55,260 --> 00:10:56,800
Nope, still lost.

176
00:10:56,960 --> 00:10:59,437
You're even dumber than
I thought you were.

177
00:10:59,520 --> 00:11:01,620
I play Big Bang Blow.

178
00:11:02,220 --> 00:11:04,580
Then I'll add my Overboost.

179
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:09,120
And last but not least, Active Guard.

180
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:11,520
And now for the fun part.

181
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:13,520
Go, Armored Gravitation!

182
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:21,780
Say, what?

183
00:11:22,540 --> 00:11:24,200
What's with the space suit?

184
00:11:45,940 --> 00:11:49,560
Each piece of my armor may
have zero attack points,

185
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:52,437
but together they form
an unstoppable force.

186
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:57,480
And as soon as I attack, you'll
experience that power for yourself.

187
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:09,740
The time draws near, my pet.

188
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,520
Be patient.

189
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:17,360
My Orichalco soldiers are gathering the
energy necessary to fuel your rebirth.

190
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:22,000
Then we'll cleanse the earth of its
impurities and rebuild paradise.

191
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:28,226
We're only one mile from
Paradis headquarters.

192
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:32,100
We'll have our company back
in no time. Right, bro?

193
00:12:32,400 --> 00:12:33,580
Don't be so sure.

194
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,317
We're dealing with an extremely
powerful organization,

195
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:40,677
and it's going to take everything
we have to bring them down.

196
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,060
This won't be easy.

197
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:46,750
All right.

198
00:12:46,960 --> 00:12:48,420
I'm officially lost.

199
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:54,000
I guess I can pretty much
forget about finding Joey now.

200
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,100
You again?

201
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:02,880
Hi, remember me?

202
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,070
Tristan!

203
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:08,780
What's going on?

204
00:13:08,940 --> 00:13:11,881
Maybe we should get someone
else behind the wheel.

205
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:15,580
Tristan needs our help.

206
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:16,990
Huh?

207
00:13:17,073 --> 00:13:17,903
Oh no!

208
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:19,640
Come on!

209
00:13:19,820 --> 00:13:21,585
I'll take whatever you've got!

210
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:23,940
Go, Celtic Guardians!

211
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,430
Tristan!

212
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:32,220
Thanks, Uke.

213
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:34,097
You came in the nick of time.

214
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:36,277
Of course, I could have taken him myself.

215
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,337
I'm afraid the only thing
that would have been

216
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:41,100
taken is your soul had
we arrived any later.

217
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:43,840
So those things are working for darts.

218
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:45,400
Hey, where's Joey?

219
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,117
I thought you guys were together.

220
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,030
We were,

221
00:13:48,113 --> 00:13:50,697
until he decided to hop
on some guy's motorcycle

222
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:53,357
and take off after one of
Darts' little flunkies.

223
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:55,040
You're kidding. Oh, no!

224
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:58,080
Was it Valon? Who? Valon.

225
00:13:58,180 --> 00:14:00,180
He's the guy Rebecca and I dueled.

226
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:01,496
Is that a bad thing?

227
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:04,477
Not only does Valon have
a thing against Joey,

228
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:07,777
but he's got a deck full of
monsters I've never seen before.

229
00:14:07,860 --> 00:14:08,690
Let's go.

230
00:14:08,773 --> 00:14:11,151
We have to find Joey before it's too late.

231
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:15,837
That chump's gonna have to wait,
because we've got bigger problems.

232
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:17,260
What do you mean?

233
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:18,780
Look around you.

234
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:25,400
That's not good.

235
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:27,240
We're surrounded.

236
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:34,880
If anyone has a plan, please speak now.

237
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:39,400
Opponent identified.

238
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:43,560
This guy just summoned
five monsters at once.

239
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:47,897
And now he's wearing them like some
kind of space-age suit of armor.

240
00:14:47,980 --> 00:14:49,140
You're out of luck.

241
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:54,320
Not only does my suit defend me, it
packs a pretty mean offense, too. What?

242
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:58,137
Your little Halloween costume
doesn't have one single attack point.

243
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:00,720
Sounds like a pretty lame offense to me.

244
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:02,155
We'll see about that.

245
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:05,160
Let's start with my right arm, shall we?

246
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,820
This part of my armor is
known as Big Bang Blow.

247
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:12,631
And I'm afraid your little
reptile's about to find out why.

248
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:16,420
Now to calculate the odds of my success.

249
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:17,620
System activate.

250
00:15:19,560 --> 00:15:23,620
Probability of monster destruction, 99%.

251
00:15:24,620 --> 00:15:26,020
Just what I thought.

252
00:15:26,680 --> 00:15:29,440
Big Bang Blow, attack alligator sword.

253
00:15:29,780 --> 00:15:32,460
That metal arm has zero attack points.

254
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:34,137
What's this guy thinking?

255
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:36,100
Alligator sword, attack!

256
00:15:38,260 --> 00:15:40,357
I don't need attack points.

257
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:44,860
Big Bang Blow automatically
destroys every monster on the field.

258
00:15:45,520 --> 00:15:46,700
No way!

259
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:49,040
I'm afraid so!

260
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:56,080
Disintegrate his lizard
with Fist of Armour!

261
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:04,100
Initiating active guard.

262
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:07,180
Absorbing attack damage.

263
00:16:09,440 --> 00:16:10,800
Not bad, eh?

264
00:16:11,400 --> 00:16:13,518
You mind telling me what's going on?

265
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:16,040
Why did I just lose 1,500 life points?

266
00:16:16,320 --> 00:16:18,261
I'll make it real simple for you.

267
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:22,377
When my right arm activates, it
destroys every monster on the field.

268
00:16:22,460 --> 00:16:25,677
Then the total number of attack
points of every monster that was

269
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:30,280
just destroyed gets subtracted from
each player's life points. Hold on.

270
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:32,297
Why didn't you lose any points?

271
00:16:32,380 --> 00:16:34,180
Because of my active guard.

272
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:37,277
Its special ability allows my
chest plate to absorb all the

273
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:40,657
damage that would have reduced
my life point so I stay safe.

274
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:41,681
That's not fair.

275
00:16:42,700 --> 00:16:44,240
Attack phase has ended.

276
00:16:44,660 --> 00:16:46,180
Disengage armor matrix.

277
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:53,560
My armor may be gone, but I
haven't lost a single life point.

278
00:16:53,860 --> 00:16:57,180
And I've got plenty more
surprises where that came from.

279
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:59,880
You'll never survive this, dual wheeler.

280
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:06,900
That's the sloppiest finish I ever saw.

281
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:12,465
Come on, you just ended your turn with no
cards on the field to protect yourself.

282
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,566
I don't need to hide
behind anything, Wheeler.

283
00:17:15,820 --> 00:17:19,080
I win all my duels by
facing my enemy head on.

284
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:22,935
That's a lesson I learned
the hard way a long time ago.

285
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:25,200
My use.

286
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:27,397
All right, you shall have that end.

287
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:28,760
Take nothing off him.

288
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,660
Here he is, sir.

289
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:33,240
Go on.

290
00:17:33,460 --> 00:17:39,040
Young Valon, you've been in and out of 12
detention centers, but mine's different.

291
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:41,240
Let me show you what I mean.

292
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:46,440
We have more productive ways of
dealing with troubled boys like you.

293
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:52,340
Try channeling your energy into these
Duel Monsters cards instead of your fists.

294
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:56,900
What he didn't tell me was he
had friends in high places.

295
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:08,857
That detention center
had a silent partner who

296
00:18:08,940 --> 00:18:12,116
showed a great deal of
interest in our dueling skills.

297
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,500
So how'd you do, kid?

298
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:17,420
Why don't you tell me?

299
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,400
You couldn't have beaten all these guys.

300
00:18:21,680 --> 00:18:23,040
The cards don't lie.

301
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:27,000
Not bad at all.

302
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,560
You want to be next?

303
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:32,760
I must say I like your
attitude, young man.

304
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:36,297
But your talents are being
wasted on this secluded island.

305
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:38,145
So why don't you come with me?

306
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:39,430
Hold on.

307
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:43,877
You're saying I can just walk away
from here with you and never come back?

308
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:46,877
Well, provided that you work
for my company, of course.

309
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,837
You got yourself a deal, Ponytail.

310
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:51,744
Just watch yourself or I
may decide to duel you.

311
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:58,977
Ever since the day he rescued me from
that dump, I've been working for darts.

312
00:18:59,060 --> 00:19:01,797
But unlike some of my
less talented colleagues,

313
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:04,800
I duel on my own terms,
just like I always have.

314
00:19:05,080 --> 00:19:07,380
And today, I'm not fighting for dogs.

315
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,980
I'm fighting for me.

316
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:15,001
This selfish punk doesn't know the
first thing about Duel Monsters.

317
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:18,771
This game is about way more
than just winning for yourself.

318
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:22,097
It's about fighting for
the people you care about.

319
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:24,600
So please, hang in there, Mike.

320
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:28,617
It's time for me to teach you
a lesson Joey Wheeler style.

321
00:19:28,700 --> 00:19:29,640
So let's go!

322
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,697
You're gonna be sorry you
ever messed with my friends!

323
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:34,610
Then let's go!

324
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:36,580
I was just getting warmed up!

325
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:40,380
Wait till you see what my
deck of armor can really do!
